WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(applause)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- All right, y'all.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.702
We have reached the end of the hour,

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.110
but I have but I have one
more uplifting story to share.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.724
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.724 --> 00:00:08.100
(energetic music)

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.930
If you can see it, you can be it.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.110
That's the idea behind a line
of female firefighter dolls.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.010
These are so cute.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.080
They were created by an actual firefighter

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.820
who says girls used to approach her

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.090
saying they didn't know women
could actually do this job.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.590
It motivate, I love these dolls.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.290
It motivated her to design dolls like this

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.630
that would inspire
girls from an early age.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.480
We have her on the line right
now watching on NBC Miami.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.180
Everybody, please say
hello to Lt. Tina Guiler

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.391
of the Miami-Dade County Fire Rescue.

00:00:34.391 --> 00:00:36.700
(audience applauding, cheering)

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.040
- [Kelly] Hello!

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.000
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.603
- I love these dolls!

00:00:40.603 --> 00:00:43.440
Oh, my God, my girl is going to love this.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.840
Have you seen the impact
that the dolls have made?

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.400
- Yes, I have.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.900
I designed them, like you said,

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.660
because I still have little
girls coming up to me

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.070
saying, "Are you really a firefighter?"

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.349
or, "I didn't know girls
could be firefighters."

00:00:55.349 --> 00:00:56.182
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:56.182 --> 00:00:57.690
- So, I thought, how am
I going to get this out

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.780
to little girls to know that
they can be firefighters, too?

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.613
- Yeah.

00:01:01.613 --> 00:01:02.580
- [Tina] So, that's why
I designed the doll.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.140
And they've been going out to kids

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.900
and I've had a mom actually come up to me

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.940
and she said, "I have
to tell you this story

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.140
about my daughter."

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:10.973
And I go, "Okay."

00:01:10.973 --> 00:01:12.690
And she goes, "My daughter came up to me

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.970
and told me that she wanted to be a boy."

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.800
And she goes, "Why do you
want to be a boy, honey?"

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.650
And she goes, "Because I
want to be a firefighter,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.050
and you have to be a boy
to be a firefighter."

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.187
So, that just broke my heart and I said,

00:01:24.187 --> 00:01:25.890
"Okay, this is the impact

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.960
that I'm changing with these dolls."

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.640
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.010
What you just said is so
powerful and such great messaging

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.830
for kids that you can be
anything, girl or boy.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.510
I heard that you're
working on other projects,

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:37.620
as well, though, right?

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.140
- [Tina] Yeah, so, I have
three of these dolls, okay?

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.730
That's Molly that you're holding there,

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:45.780
and Molly is named after Molly Williams,

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.570
who is the first known female firefighter

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.730
in the United States back in 1815,

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:53.970
so I wanted to dedicate
this doll to Molly Williams

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.130
and her service to the fire service.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.540
She was a really good firefighter,

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.190
and I just wanted to dedicate it to her.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.400
And the other two dolls'
names are Ash and Ember.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.800
And those are just fire
reference names so that you can -

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.633
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:06.930
- ...be a little firefighter.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.810
But these dolls actually promote

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.760
to help other firefighters in need,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.130
such as cancer, on-the-job injuries.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.980
So, I started a foundation
called the Triple F Foundation

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.710
and I myself beat breast cancer.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.480
So, I wanted to help other firefighters

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.730
that might be going through the same.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:24.600
- Well, congratulations -

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.545
- [Tina] So that's what that -

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.378
- ...one, on beating breast cancer,

00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:27.930
and two, thank you so
much for your service

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.070
and what you do for us.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:29.903
(applause)

00:02:29.903 --> 00:02:30.736
- [Kelly] Thank you so much.

00:02:30.736 --> 00:02:31.569
There are no words, really.

00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:34.680
I'm liking your post right
now, and that's not all.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.290
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.270
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.940
love what you're doing to
support female firefighters,

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:42.773
so they're going to be

00:02:42.773 --> 00:02:44.820
writing Triple F a check for $1000.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:45.654
How's that sound?

00:02:45.654 --> 00:02:46.770
(applause)

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.557
- Oh, my gosh, that's amazing. Thank you.

00:02:49.557 --> 00:02:51.210
- [Kelly] No, thank you so much, Tina,

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.620
once again, for your service.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.520
Thank you.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.280
And thank you to all
our guests this hour -

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.171
(audience cheering)

00:02:56.171 --> 00:02:57.091
- ...Darius Rucker, Nikki Glaser,

00:02:57.091 --> 00:02:58.661
Ava Paige, and Lawrence Zarian.

00:02:58.661 --> 00:02:59.494
Y'all have a great day,

00:02:59.494 --> 00:03:02.070
and if it's not, try and change it.

